# P11, 2026-10-13 -- the owner's question: gamespeed read a mean of 11.6M ops/frame at P9 and 18.2M at P10 (P10 re-planned
# the tours), and the renderer-only deg table showed P11 +2.5..3.4% over P10. This puts DIFFERENT binaries on the SAME frames:
# each route's poses are dumped once, then REPLAYED into every binary -- the menu skipped by poke (B0's POKE_LEAD /
# POKE_ENTER), the view pose written at every frame start, no key held, the doors at the route's states, the player's
# health held at 100 -- and each run's EXACT average ops per game frame is (total - startup) / frames.
#
# binaries (sha256, first 16):
#   0e4582a0c8d52134  doom_e1m1_blocked54.fjm
#   63869ab4be6f2ddc  doom_e1m1_onepass56.fjm
#   05c64ee3b966d5bf  doom_e1m1_blocked57.fjm
#   837f1abaccc7e7c7  doom_e1m1_blocked55.fjm
#   b45aca56ce894446  doom_e1m1_onepass55.fjm
#   blocked54 = P9's ship; onepass56 = P10's ship; blocked57 = P11; blocked55 / onepass55 = P10's source BEFORE the window-walker
#   fix (557d239), built TWO-PASS / ONE-PASS (the walker bug crashes them on most tours: 'collines run ends ... behind the fill cursor')
# routes (docs/ship-evidence/p11_ops_matrix_routes.json.gz):
#   A = P9's 10 gamespeed tours as blocked54 walked them -- scratchpad/gp/p11_trail_seen_dump.py run in a detached worktree at
#       194ed62 (P9's merge: P9's gamespeed scripts, menu and probe) on blocked54; every run ends where P9's records say
#       ((529, 208), (-296, 120), (707, 492), (147, 214), (-128, 271), (-276, 425), (-371, 80), (-452, 373), (-493, 223), (-495, 194))
#   B = P10's 10 gamespeed tours (today's binding metric) as blocked57 walked them -- the same dump at 6f9b419 on blocked57;
#       every run ends at blocked57's BINARY_ENDS
#   C = the four deg_gate viewpoints, each held 20 frames
# replay: python scratchpad/gp/p11_pose_replay.py FJM LABELS DUMP.json ...  (PYTHONPATH="src;scratchpad/12m;scratchpad/gp;scratchpad")
